# 🚀 Deal With DOM – JavaScript & Tailwind Practice

## 📌 Overview

This project represents my **tenth project**, focusing on **JavaScript DOM manipulation** combined with **Tailwind CSS** for styling.

It is a static webpage where I practiced:

- Selecting and updating DOM elements  
- Handling events (clicks, inputs, etc.)  
- Dynamically updating content  
- Integrating Tailwind CSS for quick and responsive styling  

🔗 **Live Demo:**  
https://abdelrahmangalal200101-cpu.github.io/Deal-With-DOM-JS---Assiment--10/

---

## 🛠️ Technologies Used

- HTML5  
- CSS3 (Tailwind CSS)  
- JavaScript (ES6+)  
- DOM Manipulation  

---

## 🎯 What I Learned

- How to select, modify, and remove DOM elements  
- Handling user events and updating the UI dynamically  
- Integrating Tailwind CSS with JavaScript projects  
- Writing cleaner, modular JS code for interactive pages  
- Understanding the connection between JS logic and UI behavior  

---

## 📈 Progress Note

This project highlights my **transition from static pages to interactive, dynamic web applications**.

It was a key step before diving into **React**, as it reinforced my understanding of **state, events, and component-based thinking**, which are crucial for modern frontend development.
